# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# This file was missing, and its absence was not a tidiness problem. Docker
# packages the entire directory tree before a Dockerfile runs its first
# instruction, and with the repository on a Windows drive reached through WSL's
# /mnt/c mount, that transfer runs at roughly 20 KB/s. With
# apps/frontend/node_modules at ~282 MB, `docker compose build` needed hours
# and appeared to hang -- the progress line reads "transferring context" and
# gives no hint that it is copying a dependency tree the image never uses.
#
# Nothing here is needed by any image: the frontend Dockerfile runs its own
# `npm ci`, and the Go images build from source.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build output — produced inside the image.
dist/
**/dist/
.angular/
**/.angular/

# Version control and local scratch.
.git/
.gitignore
.tmp/
*.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets. These arrive as environment variables at run time; baking them into
# an image layer would publish them with the image.
.env
*.env.local

# Test and coverage artefacts.
coverage/
**/coverage/
*.out

# Documentation and API scratch files change constantly and invalidate the
# build cache for no reason.
docs/
*.md
api.http
